@page "/services"
@layout Layout.MainLayout
@inject IServiceService ServiceSvc

<SeoHead Title="Software Engineering Services | Beldsoft"
         Description="Explore Beldsoft services for custom software, modernization, architecture, integrations, workflow automation, applied AI, cloud, and DevOps." Path="/services" />

<section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner page-hero-stacked">
        <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Services</span>
            <h1>Software engineering built around business outcomes.</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lead">From a difficult technical decision to a complete business application, Beldsoft provides focused expertise and a practical path forward.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading-wide">
            <span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span>
            <h2>Start with the constraint that matters most.</h2>
            <p>Services can stand alone or combine into a staged engagement. Discovery establishes the right scope, dependencies, responsibilities, and measures of success before delivery begins.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="services-grid">
            @foreach (var service in _services)
            {
                <article class="service-feature-card">
                    <div class="service-feature-top"><span class="card-number">@service.Id.ToString("00")</span><span class="service-category">@GetCategory(service.Id)</span></div>
                    <h2><a href="/services/@service.Slug">@service.Title</a></h2>
                    <p>@service.ShortDescription</p>
                    <ul class="mini-list" aria-label="@($"{service.Title} capabilities")">
                        @foreach (var feature in service.Features.Take(3))
                        {
                            <li>@feature</li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                    <a class="text-link" href="/services/@service.Slug" aria-label="Explore @service.Title">Explore service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
                </article>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="container section-flow">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading-wide">
            <span class="eyebrow">Choosing where to begin</span>
            <h2>You do not need a fully formed technical specification.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose readable-copy">
            <p>A useful first conversation identifies what is happening today, who is affected, which systems or processes are involved, and what a better outcome would mean for the business.</p>
            <p>From there, Beldsoft can recommend a focused assessment, a defined implementation, or ongoing engineering support.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/pricing">Review engagement models <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
        <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Not sure which service fits?</span>
            <h2>Start with the problem, not a package.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Discuss your needs</a>
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    private IEnumerable<ServiceDto> _services = [];
    private static string GetCategory(int id) => id switch
    {
        1 => "Build",
        2 => "Improve",
        3 => "Guide",
        4 => "Connect",
        5 => "Automate",
        _ => "Operate"
    };
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => _services = await ServiceSvc.GetServicesAsync();
}
